# agent worktrees (ephemeral, created by the Agent tool isolation)
.claude/worktrees/

# ── the durable store is DATA, never source (task #90) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# `.atlas/projection.json` IS the governed knowledge and `.atlas/cas/**` are its bytes. Committing them
# ships rows with any `nodeKey`, any `scope`, any `contentHash` and blobs with any `tier` — past every
# governed door, because no door is involved in a `git add`. `.atlas/staging.json` (ADR-0008) is worse in
# kind, not better: unratified LLM-proposed candidates.
# Deny-by-default, then re-include: `.atlas/*` ignores EVERY child (so a sidecar added later is ignored
# the day it appears, not the day someone remembers), and the negation below re-admits the one file that
# is genuinely source. Order matters — the negation must come AFTER the pattern it overrides. Note that
# `.atlas/` itself is deliberately NOT ignored: git cannot re-include a path under an excluded directory,
# so ignoring the directory would make the negation unreachable and silently drop `policy.json`.
.atlas/*
# …except the admin-owned policy: it is the ratified config the doors READ, and it must stay in git so a
# change to who may write what is reviewable in the same place as the code.
!.atlas/policy.json
